From: Gyuyoung Kim <qkim@google.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:10:36 -0700
Subject: [M150-LTS][MediaStream] Fix UAF in
 MediaStream(Audio|Video)Track::StopAndNotify
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stopping a track stops the corresponding source if the track was the
last one connected to the source. Stopping the source synchronously
dispatches the `ended` event on other MediaStreamTrackImpls sharing
that source, which runs script and can trigger an Oilpan GC.
If nothing else references the MediaStreamComponentImpl owning
the platform track, the compoenent's pre-finalizer
(MediaStreamComponentImpl::Dispose) deletes the platform track while
StopAndNotify() is still on the stack.

In that case, the platform track destructor has already called Stop()
(ending sinks and invalidating weak pointers), so check a `WeakPtr`
acquired before stopping the track and return early if the platform
track has been deleted.

(The merge Conflicts were fixed when the CL was cherry-picked by the ChromeOS LTS Merging Team.)

(cherry picked from commit 29268f92bbf3b2a2c5566bab2eb4d16b0e5bee49)

